      "writtenOn": "2024-06-28T17:11:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Paint and renderstep uniforms are always handled the same (SSBO if supported, UBO if no storage buffer support). Gradient buffers only work with SSBOs *and* if the float array can be packed tightly so we can have 3 possible scenarios that are all valid:\n\nNo SSBO support, so paint/renderstep uniforms are UBOs and the gradient buffer shaders are never used.\nSSBO support but using std140 layout, so paint/renderstep uniforms use SSBOs but the gradient buffer isn\u0027t used.\nSSBO support and we use std430, so everything can be in storage buffers",
      "parentUuid": "fba4fc2e_06553aec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 941,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 943,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "22f006415c334f207f6314ae04644a4bb6384fcf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
